# GitHub Linguist configuration
# =============================================================================
# Linguist measures languages by BYTES, not by files. The three analysis
# notebooks are committed with their outputs so they render on GitHub without
# being run, which means each one embeds its rendered charts as base64 PNG
# data: 4.2 MB of notebooks against 222 KB of actual Python source.
#
# Left alone, that reports the repository as 95% "Jupyter Notebook" — a
# statement about the file format rather than about the work. The notebooks'
# code cells are Python too, and every algorithm they call lives in src/prisk.
#
# Marking them as documentation keeps them fully viewable, searchable and
# diffable on GitHub while letting the language bar reflect the source.
*.ipynb linguist-documentation

# Generated artefacts: produced by `python -m prisk.pipeline`, versioned so
# that results are reproducible, but not hand-written. Excluding them keeps
# the language statistics honest and collapses their diffs by default, so a
# regenerated run does not bury a code review under thousands of changed
# numbers.
outputs/**              linguist-generated
data/processed/**       linguist-generated
data/raw/*.csv          linguist-generated
docs/img/**             linguist-generated

# Treat notebooks as text so diffs are at least inspectable.
*.ipynb text

# Normalise line endings for source and text files.
*.py     text diff=python
*.md     text
*.yaml   text
*.toml   text
*.txt    text
*.csv    text

# Binary assets.
*.png    binary
